{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780872322,"nonce":"QWfl/NPe/OMt8NZ8y627O8BURIE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABErcqjw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/234","origin":"github"},"title":"Wire Garmin GCV-20 sidescan into BizzyBoat (launch wrapper + recording)","message":"## Summary\n\nWire the Garmin GCV-20 sidescan driver into BizzyBoat: a platform launch wrapper\n(boat namespace, frame prefix, proxy IPs, sound-speed safety topic), an opt-in\ninclude in `core_launch.py`, and recording in the sonar bag.\n\nThe driver is generic (rolker/marine_tools#17, #20); per the house pattern the\nboat-specific wiring lives here, like `sound_speed_launch.py` does for the AML SVS.\n\n## Data path\n\nGCV-20 is on the Garmin Marine Network reachable from **mercat** (Windows), but\nthe ROS driver runs on **gabby**. `garmin_marine_network_proxy.ps1` (shipped with\nthe driver) bridges them — run it on mercat (defaults already match: `--gcv-ip\n172.16.3.0`, `--listen-ip 192.168.20.8`, `--relay-to 192.168.20.5`). On gabby the\ndriver points at the proxy: `gcv_ip=192.168.20.8`, `iface_ip=192.168.20.5`. The\non-net chartplotter handles GCV wake/master.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `bizzyboat_project11/launch/sidescan_launch.py` — runs the `garmin_sidescan`\n  node under `sensors/sidescan` with `frame_id=\u003cprefix\u003egarmin_sidescan`, the proxy\n  IPs, and `sound_speed_topic=/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed` (the safety\n  interlock; that topic is already published by `sound_speed_launch.py`).\n- `core_launch.py` — include it behind a `sidescan` arg (**default false**, since\n  it depends on the mercat proxy and is a parallel effort; opt in with\n  `sidescan:=true`).\n- `config/bizzyboat.yaml` — add the sidescan image topics (+ state/status, +\n  `debug/raw_status` for offline depth-decode) to `sonar_logger`.\n\nTF frames are added separately in rolker/ben_description#13. Transmit stays OFF\nby default and gated on valid sound speed.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}